  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "In a trapezium, one of the parallel sides is 4 cm longer than the other.\nThe perpendicular height is 2 cm longer than the shorter parallel side.\nThe length of the shorter parallel side is $x$ cm. The area of the trapezium is $49\\text{ cm}^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q17-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Draw a diagram and show that $x^2+4x-45=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$49=\\dfrac{(x+2)(x+x+4)}{2}=(x+2)^2$, giving $x^2+4x-45=0$.",
          "worked": "The parallel sides are $x$ cm and $(x+4)$ cm; the perpendicular height is $(x+2)$ cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{h(a+b)}{2}\\\\49&=\\frac{(x+2)(x+x+4)}{2}\\\\49&=(x+2)^2\\\\49&=x^2+4x+4\\\\x^2+4x-45&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p17-q17-a-solution-diagram",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 17 question 17a\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (B) at (5,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (4,2.5);\n\\coordinate (D) at (1,2.5);\n\\coordinate (H) at (1,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (D)--(H);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] ($(H)!0.12!(B)$)--($(H)!0.12!(B)+(0,0.3)$)--($(H)+(0,0.3)$);\n\\path (D)--(C) node[midway,above,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] {$x\\text{ cm}$};\n\\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] {$(x+4)\\text{ cm}$};\n\\path (D)--(H) node[midway,right,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] {$(x+2)\\text{ cm}$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 65,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 17,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 17a student drawing response",
                "description": "Authored schematic trapezium with horizontal parallel sides and a dashed perpendicular height. Shape is not to scale; no additional numerical givens are introduced.",
                "mathematics": "Parallel sides x and x+4 cm; perpendicular height x+2 cm.",
                "answerVisibility": "Solution only; the student must draw the diagram."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 82
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q17-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=5$, so the shorter parallel side is 5 cm. Reject $x=-9$ because a length must be positive.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+4x-45&=0\\\\(x+9)(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=-9\\text{ or }5\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x>0$, $x=5$. The shorter parallel side is 5 cm.\nCheck: the other parallel side is 9 cm and the height is 7 cm, so $\\dfrac{7(5+9)}{2}=49\\text{ cm}^2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
